   "title": "DPK welcomes Lee's budget speech; PPP slams failure to address N. Korea, economic woes",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/politics/20261102/dpk-welcomes-lees-budget-speech-ppp-slams-failure-to-address-n-korea-economic-woes",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 08:57:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793609823.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "The ruling Democratic Party of Korea (DPK) on Monday welcomed President Lee Jae Myung's budget speech, while the main opposition People Power Party (PPP) criticized him for failing to address North Korea's threats and economic concerns. PPP lawmakers also staged a rally at the National Assembly ahead of Lee's speech on next year's budget proposal, condemning what they called a budget that disregards national debt and destroys the country's future.",
   "summary_zh": "朝鲜执政党民主劳动党（DPK）于星期一欢迎总统李在明的预算演讲，而主要反对党国民力量党（PPP）则批评他未能处理朝鲜的威胁和经济忧虑。国民力量党议员还在李发表下一年度预算提案演讲之前，于国民议会举行集会，谴责他们所称的无视国家债务并毁掉国家未来的预算。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The ruling Democratic Party of Korea (DPK) on Monday welcomed President Lee Jae Myung's budget speech, while the main opposition People Power Party (PPP) criticized him for failing to address North Korea's threats and economic concerns. PPP lawmakers also staged a rally at the National Assembly ahead of Lee's speech on next year's budget proposal, condemning what they called a budget that disregards national debt and destroys the country's future. \"President Lee came, said only what he wanted to say and left,\" PPP leader Jang Dong-hyeok wrote on Facebook. \"He made no mention of real estate, the stock market or farmland, nor did he mention North Korea, the South Korea-U.S. alliance, public safety or judicial issues,\" Rep. Jang said. While Lee pledged to secure key military capabilities needed for the early transfer of wartime operational control (OPCON) from the United States, he did not directly mention the alliance or inter-Korean ties in his speech. \"President Lee's parliamentary speech was not a blueprint for restoring people's livelihoods but an irresponsible declaration of financial gambling that puts the future of South Korea at stake,\" Rep. Park said in a commentary. Meanwhile, the ruling party welcomed Lee's speech, vowing to pass the budget proposal by the Dec. 2 deadline. On his social media, DPK leader Kim Min-seok hailed the speech for presenting an \"ambitious vision\" of transforming South Korea into an \"irreplaceable\" global leader, stressing the need to ensure that the benefits of economic growth are shared by all. \"As the president emphasized, we must make every effort to overcome inequality and polarization,\" Kim wrote on X. During his speech, Lee pledged bold investment in artificial intelligence (AI) and other future growth engine industries, calling for bipartisan support for the government's proposed record budget of 820.9 trillion won ($614.5 billion) for next year. The proposed amount marks a 12.8 percent increase from this year's budget, the highest growth rate on record",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "kr"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "eco",
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
