   "title": "Seoul Plaza to host night market Friday featuring 47 small businesses",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/lifestyle/people-events/20261102/seoul-plaza-to-host-night-market-friday-featuring-47-small-businesses",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 08:57:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793609823.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Seoul Plaza will turn into an evening marketplace Friday, offering shoppers a chance to discover products from 47 small businesses, enjoy live performances and receive discounts as the city looks to bring more spending into the nighttime economy. The Seoul Metropolitan Government will hold its 2026 Small Business Day celebration from 10 a.m. to 9 p.m. Friday, extending operating hours by two hours from last year to accommodate office workers and other visitors unable to attend during the day.",
   "summary_zh": "首尔广场将于周五变身夜间市集，为购物者提供发现47家小企业产品的机会，并可欣赏现场表演、享受折扣；市政府希望借此推动更多消费流入夜间经济。首尔 Metropolitan Government 将于周五上午10时至晚上9时举行2026年小企业日庆祝活动，在去年的基础上延长营业时间两小时，以方便无法在白天参加的白领及其他访客。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Seoul Plaza will turn into an evening marketplace Friday, offering shoppers a chance to discover products from 47 small businesses, enjoy live performances and receive discounts as the city looks to bring more spending into the nighttime economy. The Seoul Metropolitan Government will hold its 2026 Small Business Day celebration from 10 a.m. to 9 p.m. Friday, extending operating hours by two hours from last year to accommodate office workers and other visitors unable to attend during the day. The event marks Small Business Day, observed annually on Nov. 5, and carries the theme \"Better everyday lives created by small shops, Seoul as a city of quality living.\" Participating businesses will offer products ranging from meal kits, premium teas and baked goods to handmade soaps, accessories, leather goods and traditional crafts. Fifteen businesses that have benefited from Seoul's startup and market development support programs will also participate, giving them an opportunity to introduce their products to new customers. Shoppers can receive a 10 percent discount by purchasing the event-exclusive Small Business Happiness Gift Certificate through the Seoul Pay Plus mobile app beginning at 10 a.m. on Friday. The certificates can be used at participating market booths throughout the event. The program will also feature live fusion \"gukak\" music, jazz and acoustic music from 6 p.m. to 8:40 p.m., following magic and jazz performances beginning at 3 p.m. Free activities, including caricature drawing, face painting and photography, will be available from 11 a.m. to 6 p.m., while visitors can collect stamps at participating booths for small business products and souvenirs. A ceremony at 4 p.m. will honor 24 recipients for contributions to the local economy, including 20 outstanding small business owners and four exemplary business operators. This article was published with the assistance of generative AI and edited by The Korea Times",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "kr"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "eco"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
