   "title": "LG Electronics CEO eyes 'caregiving' as next frontier for AI-powered homes",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/business/companies/20261102/lg-electronics-ceo-eyes-caregiving-as-next-frontier-for-ai-powered-homes",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 08:57:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793609823.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "The chief of LG Electronics said on Monday that \"caregiving\" could become the next frontier for artificial intelligence (AI)-powered services. In a post on his LinkedIn account, Chief Executive Officer (CEO) Lyu Jae-cheol outlined the company's vision for AI-powered homes, saying they should go beyond simply adding AI features to connected devices.",
   "summary_zh": "LG Electronics首席执行官周一表示，“照护”可能成为人工智能（AI）驱动服务的下一个前沿领域。首席执行官（CEO）吕在哲在其LinkedIn账号上发帖阐述公司对人工智能驱动家居的愿景，称这类家居应超越仅仅为联网设备添加人工智能功能。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The chief of LG Electronics said on Monday that \"caregiving\" could become the next frontier for artificial intelligence (AI)-powered services. In a post on his LinkedIn account, Chief Executive Officer (CEO) Lyu Jae-cheol outlined the company's vision for AI-powered homes, saying they should go beyond simply adding AI features to connected devices. \"This is the direction envisioned by LG Electronics' 'Zero-Labor Home' vision, which aims to free people from household chores,\" Lyu said. The Korean home appliance maker has been spearheading efforts to transform the way people manage their homes through its AI-powered appliance lineup, ranging from refrigerators to air purifiers. Rather than simply adding AI functions to connected devices, the goal should be to fundamentally change the way homes operate, he said. Lyu emphasized, however, that AI-powered homes should reduce the burden of repetitive household chores while leaving important decisions in the hands of users",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
