   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Police have registered an FIR in connection with alleged graffiti on a police vehicle during the INDIA bloc's November 1 rally at the Ramlila Maidan in Delhi, an official said on Monday (November 2, 2026). ‘Vote chor’ graffiti, littered roads, and a muddy ‘catwalk’ at Ramlila Maidan after INDIA bloc rally The FIR was registered at Kamla Market police station under sections of the Delhi Prevention of Defacement of Property Act, they said.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。警方已就印度民主联盟（INDIA）11月1日在德里拉姆利拉广场举行集会期间，警方车辆遭涂鸦一事登记首次信息报告（FIR），一名官员于周一（2026年11月2日）表示。据称，拉姆利拉广场在INDIA联盟集会后出现了“Vote chor”（意为“投票作弊”）涂鸦、散落道路的垃圾以及泥泞的“猫步”。警方称，这份首次信息报告已在卡姆拉市场警察站登记，适用《德里防止财产污损法》的相关条款。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Police have registered an FIR in connection with alleged graffiti on a police vehicle during the INDIA bloc's November 1 rally at the Ramlila Maidan in Delhi, an official said on Monday (November 2, 2026). ‘Vote chor’ graffiti, littered roads, and a muddy ‘catwalk’ at Ramlila Maidan after INDIA bloc rally The FIR was registered at Kamla Market police station under sections of the Delhi Prevention of Defacement of Property Act, they said. According to police, several videos showing graffiti on the police vehicle have gone viral on social media. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
