   "title": "Rising Printing, Distribution Costs Threatening Nigerian Newspapers–Publisher",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/rising-printing-distribution-costs-threatening-nigerian-newspapers-publisher/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 08:37:49 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793608669.0,
   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "He said the cost of printing newspapers had risen significantly, while the expenses involved in distributing publications across cities nationwide had more than tripled following the increase in fuel prices. “The cost of printing newspapers is seriously on the high side at the moment. The publisher also identified the difficulty in attracting advertisements as another major challenge, noting that advertising remained a primary source of revenue for newspaper organisations.",
   "summary_zh": "他说，印刷报纸的成本已大幅上涨，而燃油价格上涨后，将出版物分发至全国各城市的相关费用也增至原来的三倍以上。“目前印刷报纸的成本严重偏高。出版商还指出，难以吸引广告是另一项重大挑战，并表示广告仍是报纸机构的主要收入来源。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Dickson, who spoke to LEADERSHIP, called on the federal government to subsidise the cost of newsprint to ease the financial burden on publishers. He said the cost of printing newspapers had risen significantly, while the expenses involved in distributing publications across cities nationwide had more than tripled following the increase in fuel prices. “The cost of printing newspapers is seriously on the high side at the moment. We actually think the government can, in a way, subsidise the cost of newsprint. It will go a very long way in bringing down the cost of printing newspapers,” he said. The publisher also identified the difficulty in attracting advertisements as another major challenge, noting that advertising remained a primary source of revenue for newspaper organisations. According to him, even established media organisations are struggling to attract advertisements, leaving smaller publishers with greater difficulties in generating income. Dickson said the financial challenges had also affected the organisation’s capacity to expand its workforce, disclosing that it currently had about 15 staff members across the country. He expressed hope that the organisation would employ more people as its revenue improves. Meanwhile, Authentic News Daily has been named Media Agency of the Year at the 2026 League of Extraordinary Achievers Awards (LEAA), organised by Gaze Production. The award ceremony is scheduled to hold on Sunday, December 6, 2026, at Hotel Seventeen, Tafawa Balewa Way, Kaduna. Established in 2015 as an online news platform, Authentic News Daily has expanded into print publishing, with its newspapers circulating in major cities across Nigeria. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
