   "title": "Galamsey fight: Chinese have invaded our forest",
   "url": "https://www.mynewsgh.com/galamsey-fight-chinese-have-invaded-our-forest-suame-mp-alleges",
   "domain": "mynewsgh.com",
   "source": "mynewsgh.com",
   "published": "Sun, 01 Nov 2026 22:06:44 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793570804.0,
   "ageDays": 0.47,
   "summary": "Suame MP John Darko has questioned the government’s claim that it is unaware of Chinese nationals operating at Narawa Mines, insisting that their visible presence and alleged military protection make such a position difficult to accept. Speaking on TV3’s Keypoint, the New Patriotic Party (NPP) MP said the government could not reasonably deny knowledge of the Chinese nationals when videos showing their activities at the mining site were already circulating.",
   "summary_zh": "苏阿梅选区议员约翰·达科对政府声称不知道中国人在纳拉瓦矿场作业的说法提出质疑，坚持认为，中国人员公开可见且据称受到军方保护，政府很难接受这种说法。新爱国党议员在TV3《关键点》节目中表示，鉴于显示中国人在矿区活动的视频已经在网上流传，政府无法合理地否认自己知道这些中国人的存在。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Suame MP John Darko has questioned the government’s claim that it is unaware of Chinese nationals operating at Narawa Mines, insisting that their visible presence and alleged military protection make such a position difficult to accept. Speaking on TV3’s Keypoint, the New Patriotic Party (NPP) MP said the government could not reasonably deny knowledge of the Chinese nationals when videos showing their activities at the mining site were already circulating. “Chinese have invaded our forest and you are sitting here telling us that government is not aware. That is even worse,” he said. He argued that the Chinese nationals had gone beyond merely appearing at the mining site, claiming that they were constructing roads and putting up facilities. “There are videos of these Chinese in this mining area. They are building facilities, they are constructing roads, and we’ve seen the videos. And all government can say is that we are not aware. The guy says we are working for government, and you are claiming you are not aware,” he added. Darko said the situation raised serious questions about the government’s knowledge of the activities taking place at the mine, particularly the alleged relationship between the Chinese nationals and the military personnel providing security. “The Chinese are there with military protection. You are telling me that government has no idea as to how the Chinese and the military are working together?” he questioned. He warned that if the government genuinely had no knowledge of the developments, it would point to a serious failure in oversight and the management of the country’s natural resources. “We cannot sit here and pretend that government doesn’t know anything about it. In fact, if that is the position, then we are dead as a country. It means that we have foreigners invading our forest and we have a sleepy government,” he said. Mahama’s team believes in indigenisation only when it benefits them – MP Narawa Mines termination: Go to court to recover the debt – John Darko How Ghana, Lebanon collaborated to arrest Syrian national with 40kg cocaine at Beirut Airport Galamsey financiers fund political activities, so how can politicians hold them accountable? – Solomon Owusu UP will charge parliamentary aspirants only Ghc1 for filing fee – Solomon Owusu Alan will contest the 2028 elections on the UP ticket – Solomon Owusu declares You said you would resign – Miracles Aboagye reminds Ablakwa over private jet pledge 761 people have not been accounted for – NPP challenges Ablakwa over evacuation records This site uses Akismet to reduce spam. Learn how your comment data is processed. A woman has vowed to make her husband impotent after accusing him of maltreatment and infidelity, claiming that she supported... Prophet Nana Akwesi Amponsah has called on churches to put instrumentalists on their payroll and pay them for their services, arguing... Founder of the Hope Generation Ministry International, Prophet Nana Akwesi Amponsah, known widely as Computer Man, has criticised what he... The Judicial Service Staff Association of Ghana (JUSAG) has declared an indefinite strike from Monday, November 2, 2026, after months... The Mayor of the Kumasi Metropolitan Assembly (KMA), Richard Ofori Agyemang Boadi, has challenged the Minority to provide evidence of... President John Mahama has urged Ghanaians to criticise government decisions whenever they believe the country is being taken in the... President John Mahama has disclosed that he regularly monitors complaints about government performance on social media platforms, including TikTok, and... Renowned Dermatologist and Founder of Rabito Clinic, Prof. Edmund Delle, has highlighted how much people, particularly women, value their appearance,... Founder of Rabito Clinic, Naa Prof. Edmund Delle, has recounted the unusual story of how the clinic received rabbits as... The Acting Commissioner for Rent Control, Mr Frederick Opoku, has been praised for his efforts to enforce rent regulations and... Nearly $200m invested before disputed takeover – Northern Ashanti Mines My greatest fear in this world was going to prison – Wontumi Speaks from Nsawam NAIMOS operation leaves 400 Northern Ashanti Mines workers on standby Leaked GTA memo: Whoever brought it out has to be sanctioned – Jantuah",
