   "title": "FG Tasks Nigerians On Use Of Locally Made Technology For Economic Growth",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/fg-tasks-nigerians-on-use-of-locally-made-technology-for-economic-growth/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sun, 01 Nov 2026 05:11:39 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793509899.0,
   "ageDays": 1.17,
   "summary": "The Executive Vice Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of the National Agency for Science and Engineering Infrastructure (NASENI), Mr Khalil Suleiman Halilu, made the call during the distribution of solar home systems, clean cooking stoves and household support packs to 330 residents of Ondo State in Akure. Halilu said the initiative was designed to translate research and development into practical products that could improve living conditions and provide economic opportunities for Nigerians.",
   "summary_zh": "尼日利亚国家科学与工程基础设施局执行副主席兼首席执行官Khalil Suleiman Halilu先生在阿库雷向奥多州330名居民分发太阳能家庭系统、清洁炉灶和家庭支持包时提出这一倡议。Halilu表示，该计划旨在将研究成果转化为实用产品，以改善尼日利亚人的生活条件并为其创造经济机会。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Executive Vice Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of the National Agency for Science and Engineering Infrastructure (NASENI), Mr Khalil Suleiman Halilu, made the call during the distribution of solar home systems, clean cooking stoves and household support packs to 330 residents of Ondo State in Akure. Halilu said the initiative was designed to translate research and development into practical products that could improve living conditions and provide economic opportunities for Nigerians. He explained that the solar home systems would provide lighting for households, enable children to study at night and support small businesses, while the clean cooking stoves would offer more efficient cooking alternatives and reduce exposure to smoke when properly used. According to him, wider adoption of locally developed products would encourage domestic manufacturing and strengthen Nigeria’s capacity to develop solutions to its own challenges. He said “This is to promote locally produced items which brings about employment and also to have something good for our communities. He said the NASENI Sustainable Empowerment Programme had reached more than 10 states across the six geopolitical zones, with 330 men and women benefiting from the intervention in Ondo State. The NASENI chief executive added that the programme was intended to take technological innovations beyond research facilities and make them accessible to households and businesses. Also speaking, the Minister of Youth Development, Ayodele Olawande, said beneficiaries would receive additional financial support to enable them to establish or strengthen micro-businesses. Olawande said the intervention was not a political strategy but an effort to take technology-based solutions and economic opportunities to grassroots communities. In his remarks, gov. Yusuf commended Abejide for extending his empowerment programme beyond his constituency, urging other federal lawmakers to support Nigerians irrespective of their ethnic or religious backgrounds. He said such interventions would promote national unity, peaceful coexistence and economic development. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "eco",
    "ene"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": false,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
   "score": 0.6,
   "tag": "rss_leadership",
   "title_zh": "联邦政府敦促尼日利亚人使用本土制造的技术促进经济增长",
   "body_zh": "国家科学与工程基础设施局（NASENI）执行副主席兼首席执行官Khalil Suleiman Halilu先生，在阿库雷向奥 ND州330名居民分发太阳能家庭系统、清洁炊具和家居支持包时发出了这一号召。Halilu表示，该倡议旨在将研究与开发成果转化为实用产品，以改善生活条件，并为尼日利亚人提供经济机会。他解释说，太阳能家庭系统将为家庭提供照明，使儿童能够在夜间学习，并支持小型企业；正确使用时，清洁炊具可提供更高效的烹饪方式，并减少烟雾暴露。据他介绍，推广本地研发产品将鼓励国内制造，增强尼日利亚自主开发应对自身挑战解决方案的能力。他说：“这是为了推广本地生产的产品，既能带来就业，也能让我们的社区获得优质产品。”他说，NASENI可持续发展计划已覆盖全国六个地缘政治区域中的10多个州，其中330名男女在奥ND州受益于该项干预。NASENI首席执行官还表示，该计划旨在让技术创新走出研究机构，使家庭和企业都能获得这些成果。青年发展部长Ayodele Olawande也表示，受益者将获得额外财政支持，以便创办或强化微型企业。Olawande称，这项干预并非政治策略，而是旨在把基于技术的解决方案和经济机会带到基层社区。在发言中，州长Yusuf赞扬Abejide将其赋能计划延伸至选区之外，并敦促其他联邦议员不论尼日利亚人的族裔或宗教背景，都向其提供支持。他说，此类干预将促进国家团结、和平共处和经济发展。我们掌握独家优势。实时报道、突发独家新闻和独家视角将直接发送到您的手机。不要满足于过时新闻。加入LEADERSHIP NEWS WhatsApp频道，获取全天候最新动态 →",
