   "url": "https://x.com/flvcovlquimistv/status/2116384753909998079",
   "snippet": "I didn't agree with her in the other clip that is going around but I do agree with this one.\n\nThe US played it too fast and loose with their ability to impose sanctions. Spit in allies faces by selling them weapons and weapons systems that only work when the US gives them permission to use them. Breaks treaties on a whim when it feels like. Abuses control of the swift system. Spent the last 65 years meddling in Latin American elections.\n\nIt's only natural that people are looking for ways to circumvent all that. I said a while back the goal for a BRICS currency almost certainly wouldnt be to challenge the dollars dominance. As long as the Euro been out it hasn't even come close. The goal is to be able to pay each other next time the US tries to sanction one of them into bending the knee.\n\nI see the increased prominence of coordination agreements like NB8, Mercosur, The Alliance of Sahel States etc to be the precursor to a multipolar world, polarized by region",
